    "preview": "Special Course - Project framing\n\nSpecial Course - Project framing\n\nTowards subject-invariant and temporally coherent end-to-end latent models for unsupervised mouse sleep staging\n\nMain aim\nBuild an end-to-end version of your thesis pipeline that:\n\nreplaces FFT-based inputs with CNN feature learning\n\nkeeps conditioning only in the decoder\n\nreplaces the static GM prior with a temporally dependent latent prior\n\ntests zero-shot transfer from decoder-only conditioning\n\nends in a 5\u201310 page paper draft\n\nCore research question\n\nCan an end-to-end convolutional autoencoding model with decoder-only conditioning and a temporally dependent latent prior learn a more transferable and subject-invariant latent space for unsupervised mouse sleep staging than the FFT-based cGMVAE pipeline?\n\nThe right structure: 3 layers\n\nLayer 1 \u2014 Invariance\n\nRemove subject conditioning from encoder\n\nKeep subject conditioning only in decoder\n\nTest true zero-shot on unseen mice without using held-out subject data during representation training\n\nLab conditioning: Use Lab 5 (E) first\n\nhas the same montages (1 parietal + 1 frontal electrode )\n\nthis has 5s epchs but has been fixed by Javi to 4s\n\nMontage conditioning: Then use lab 2 (B)\n\nhas double the channels but same montage placement (2 parietal + 2 frontal electrodes)\n\nwas 1s epochs but has been fixed by Javi to 4s\n\nIgnore lab 1 and 4 as they are not as good.\n\nThis directly targets the issue that the thesis cGMVAE population result was partially transductive because the subject-conditioned encoder used limited held-out-subject data.\n\nLayer 2 \u2014 Representation\n\nReplace FFT / expert spectral frontend with CNN encoder\n\nUse transposed convolutions in decoder\n\nTrain on consecutive windows or epoch windows from raw time-domain input\n\nCompare against thesis spectral baseline\n\nThis is well motivated because the thesis explicitly proposes incorporating time-domain inputs and possibly staged spectral-to-end-to-end training.\n\nLayer 3 \u2014 Temporal prior\n\nReplace sta"
